Based on the council's outbuilding guidance, a garden shed under 2.5 metres high usually does not need a planning application, provided that:

- It sits behind the front wall of the house (not in front of it).
- It covers less than half of the garden.

Some exceptions apply. If your property is in a conservation area or is a listed building, different rules apply and you may need to apply even for a small shed. Please also note that I can't give a formal planning opinion, so if you're unsure, it's worth checking.

If you tell me your property address, I can check whether any constraints apply to it. Alternatively, you can contact the planning desk directly for a formal answer before you build.
